window.docContents[59].resolve({"/Convex-subgroups-and-coarsening-of-valuations/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Convex-subgroups-and-coarsening-of-valuations":{"contents":"A subgroup  of a linearly ordered commutative group  is convex if\n and  force . In Adic-Spaces this is the\nstructure , and  is the smallest\nconvex subgroup containing a set . Convex subgroups of the value group control the\ncoarsenings of a valuation. Following Wedhorn §7.1.\n\nThe coarsening of a valuation  by a convex subgroup \n() is the composite  with the quotient projection. Coarser valuations have\nthe same support but a smaller value group; passing to a maximal proper convex subgroup\ngives a height-one (rank-one) coarsening. In Adic-Spaces: .\nFollowing Wedhorn §7.1.\n\nFor a valuation  and an ideal  Wedhorn singles out the convex subgroup\n generated by the values  attained by  (),\nrelative to  packaged as . This characteristic subgroup\nrecords the \"microbial\" part of the value group and is the technical device behind the\n description of continuity (). Following\nWedhorn Definition 4.13.\n\n","context":"Adic Spaces — Lean blueprint","header":"3. Convex subgroups and coarsening of valuations","id":"/Convex-subgroups-and-coarsening-of-valuations/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Convex-subgroups-and-coarsening-of-valuations"}});